  "id": "design-trade-off",
  "term": "design trade-off",
  "definition": "A design trade-off is a situation where improving one aspect of a system creates a cost in another. In this study, giving richer guidance improved coordination, comfort, and task efficiency, but it was also linked with greater cognitive and physiological demand.",
